'''termor''' (tėr′mor), ''n.'' [< ''term'' + ''-or''<sup>1</sup>.] In ''law'', one who has an estate for a term of years or for life. Also ''termer''.

'''term-piece''' (tėrm′pēs), ''n.'' Same as ''term'', 5.

